<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94818" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῐᾱγρᾰφ-ία</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>painting with the
			shadows</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκιαγραφέω</span>),  so as to produce an illusion of solidity at a
			distance, <i>scene-painting</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ἀσαφεῖ καὶ ἀπατηλῷ χρώμεθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Criti.</u>
					107d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκιαγραφίαν ἀρετῆς περιγραπτέον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					365c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				602d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Phd.</u>
				69b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Numen.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				14.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ς. καὶ τὰ ἐνύπνια</span>,
			compared as being both illusory, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1024b23
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ δημηγορικὴ λέξις ἔοικε τῇ
			ς.</span>, i.e. in being calculated for effect, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1414a8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				52.7
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
